      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "The regular price is subjected to a $20\\%$ discount, making it $\\$30(1 - 0.20) = \\$24$ for the sale price.\n\nMary's coupon then reduces this amount by $25\\%$, making the final price $\\$24(1-0.25) = \\$18$.\n\nThe merchandise is then reduced by $x\\%$ of the final price which is equal to $18 provides a single percent discount as \\begin{align*}\n30\\left(1 - \\frac{x}{100}\\right) &= 18 \\\\\n&= .90 \\cdot 30 \\\\\n(\\frac{x}{100}) &= \\frac{18}{30} \\\\\nx&= \\frac{60}{30} \\\\\nx &= \\boxed{20\\%}\n\\end{align*}. The answer is 20",
