      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "First, we find the sale price of the shirt. Since it is on sale for $20\\%$ off, and the original price was $\\$30$, the sale price is $\\$30 \\cdot (1 - 0.20) = \\$30 \\cdot 0.80 = \\$24$.\n\nNext, we find the after-coupon price by applying $25\\%$ off of the sale price. The after-coupon price is $\\$24 \\cdot (1 - 0.25) = \\$24 \\cdot 0.75 = \\$18$.\n\nFinally, we need to find the single percent discount that would give the same final price as the two successive discounts combined. \n\nThe two successive discounts are a total of $20\\% + 25\\% = 45\\%$. \n\nIf the final price is $\\$18$, this means the shirt was sold at a fixed price of $\\$18$ originally. \n\nThe single percent discount that would give this final price is $100\\% - 45\\% = \\boxed{55\\%}$. The answer is 55",
